WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:02.830
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:08.120
Today I am going to explain a short adventure
film called “In Captivity.”

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.330
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:15.230
Watch out and take care!

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:19.560
At the beginning of the movie, we are introduced
to the protagonist, Jim.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.180
He lives in a museum on humans and has never
been to the outside world.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.560
The museum is run by Cyborgs to exhibit how
humans used to live in the past.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.850
Since humans are an endangered species, Jim
is the main attraction of the museum.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:39.570
His apartment is tiny and consists of only
three rooms; a bedroom, a bathroom, and the

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.770
living area.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:46.110
There is a staircase to replicate the natural
human habitat but the stairs lead nowhere.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:50.640
Like the fake windows and doors, most of the
things in the house are props, except for

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.540
the TV that Jim likes to watch every day.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.940
In the opening scene, Jim is watching a TV
show that he knows every word to.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.219
To him, the scenario in the movie is how humans
interact in real life.

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:07.190
The Cyborgs deliberately make him watch specific
shows so he would learn how human males are

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.259
supposed to act around females.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:14.920
Jim is also devouring a pack of cereals, inside
which, he finds a rare toy prize.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.260
Not caring about the mess he makes, he excitedly
runs to the shelf that he uses to present

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.850
his cereal prizes.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.399
He places the one he found on the top and
watches it in fascination.

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:30.180
It is clear that cereals are his everyday
meal and he loves collecting the prizes.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.159
Collecting them and watching TV are his only
hobbies.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:38.409
Every day, a Cyborg museum guide brings a
group of tourist Cyborgs to show them the

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:39.409
museum.

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:44.310
They start by viewing the “everyday human
devices” area where toasters, traffic cones,

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.270
toy trains, lava lamps, and other everyday
things are exhibited.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.009
But of course, the center of attention of
the museum is Jim.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:55.289
The tourists watch him through a glass window
in his apartment.

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:59.280
The guide introduces him as the only human
raised in captivity.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.500
The Cyborg historians have tried to replicate
the habitat that humans used to live in, to

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.890
create Jim’s apartment.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.900
As the tourists watch Jim in his house, he
gives them a thumbs up.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.670
He doesn’t complain about the strangers
invading his privacy because he doesn’t

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.040
realize he is being held in captivity.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.430
Jim has always thought this is how his life
is supposed to be.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:24.140
The tourists observe and examine his behaviors
and habits like he is a test subject of their

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.140
experiment.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.980
When they are about to leave, an announcement
encourages them to return to the museum to

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.250
watch a new addition; a female human.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.710
Jim is very excited to hear this as he has
only seen human girls on TV.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.620
He is ready to meet the girl of his dreams
like he had always imagined while watching

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.990
TV shows.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.880
The next day is a joyous one for Jim.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.170
He gets up early, brushes his teeth, and takes
an extra long shower.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.980
He also sprays himself with a lot of deodorant
and dresses up in a nice suit to welcome his

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.310
new female friend.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:01.110
As he nervously waits, a beautiful girl named
Caz is brought into the apartment.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.600
Before she says anything, Jim recites dialogue
from his favorite movie, thinking it is the

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.930
best way to greet her.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.380
But Caz freaks out and starts running around
the house looking for a way out.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:16.030
Since she was captured from the outside world,
she knows she is being held captive.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.860
However, the doors and windows of Jim’s
apartment are all fake to make it look like

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.660
a real home, so she cannot run away.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.710
Caz goes to the bedroom to look for a way
out, only to see a bed decorated with rose

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:28.710
petals.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:32.650
Jim had some plans ready for her arrival,
he hasn’t learned any social skills from

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.860
the movies but knows what sexual intercourse
is.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:40.620
Caz finally sees the Cyborgs watching them
from the windows and hides behind a wall.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.820
Jim introduces himself for the first time
making Caz realize he is a human too.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:49.820
She asks him if he knows a way to get out
but Jim is confused as to why she would want

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.820
to leave.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:55.070
He claims that he has all the amazing things
in the apartment like an extendable couch

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:58.060
and the TV with over five channels on it.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:05.620
He even gets unlimited complimentary meals
and energy drinks every day.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.680
Caz is unimpressed by his version of “amazing
things”.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.260
She cries and Jim tries to console her with
a rose.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.130
At dinner time, Jim and Caz sit down to eat.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.629
Jim heats an artificial meal for her in an
oven and starts eating.

00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:22.780
But Caz is disgusted by the smell of the food.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.479
Seeing Jim enjoying it, she asks him if he
has ever been outside.

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:30.310
When he doesn’t answer, she asks him to
smell the food but Jim still doesn’t get

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.099
what she is trying to prove.

00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:37.550
Caz curses the Cyborgs who are still observing
them like bacteria under the microscope.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.740
She turns back to Jim and explains to him
that none of this is real.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:46.110
The foods do not taste what they are supposed
to taste like, the stairs do not lead anywhere,

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.879
and the front door doesn’t open more than
four inches.

00:04:48.879 --> 00:04:54.020
Jim listens to her complaints, with a smile
on his face and doesn’t say anything.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.669
When she asks him why the fake apartment doesn’t
bother him, he yawns and says he is going

00:04:58.669 --> 00:04:59.710
to sleep.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.680
He excitedly asks Caz to join him in the bed
if she wants to.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.259
Caz retreats away from him, asking why she
would go to bed with him.

00:05:07.259 --> 00:05:11.360
Jim then suggests they propagate which makes
Caz freeze in shock.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.350
She declares that she would never propagate
with him and sends him to his bedroom.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.479
Jim angrily throws away all the rose petals
from his bed and goes to sleep while the Cyborgs

00:05:20.479 --> 00:05:22.630
outside still watch him.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.409
Caz sleeps on the couch outside.

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:28.560
At midnight, Jim brings out a blanket and
puts it over Caz.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:34.100
He also goes as far as to get his best cereal
prize and keep it beside her to keep her company.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.759
Caz wakes up sometime later and sees the toy
by her side.

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:42.650
She gets an idea and uses the prize toys to
create a landscape on the glass window.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:47.449
When Jim wakes up, he is upset to see his
toys missing but his disappointment vanishes

00:05:47.449 --> 00:05:49.979
when he sees the art Caz has created.

00:05:49.979 --> 00:05:52.689
She tells him that the scenery on the glass
is her home.

00:05:52.689 --> 00:05:56.029
But Jim still claims that the apartment is
her home now.

00:05:56.029 --> 00:06:00.419
She calmly explains to him that human beings
aren’t supposed to live with the Cyborgs,

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:02.280
their home is outside.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:06.660
The following day at breakfast, Jim hides
from the Cyborgs using a plant.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:10.569
He then secretly tells Caz there is a way
to get out of the apartment.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:14.309
Every few days, an attendant with a cart comes
through the main door.

00:06:14.309 --> 00:06:18.569
Caz can hide inside the cart without him knowing
and go outside.

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:23.870
But since the cart only has space for one
person, Jim will remain stuck in the museum.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.430
Caz worriedly tells him that he doesn’t
belong here but Jim claims that he is happy

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.759
and satisfied.

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:32.809
He asks her to not worry about him and reach
home safely.

00:06:32.809 --> 00:06:37.060
At night, a Cyborg arrives with a cart to
refill the fridge.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:41.690
Caz carefully gets inside the cart and is
taken outside without anyone knowing.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:46.539
The next day, the supervisor Cyborg asks Jim
if he knows where the female human is but

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.990
Jim says he doesn’t.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:52.539
In the next museum tour, the tour guide introduces
a group of Cyborgs to Jim.

00:06:52.539 --> 00:06:57.349
However, when the couch moves around, they
see that Jim has tied a Cyborg to it and has

00:06:57.349 --> 00:06:59.120
escaped.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:04.229
In the last scene, we see Jim walk to a girl
in a field that looks exactly like the landscape

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:06.309
Caz had depicted in her art.

00:07:06.309 --> 00:07:11.729
Jim’s captivity has a striking resemblance
to how animals in zoos, circuses, and aquariums

00:07:11.729 --> 00:07:12.879
are treated.

00:07:12.879 --> 00:07:16.990
The movie keeps things in perspective for
humans on how it feels like to live away from

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.090
your own kind in an environment of “fake”
perfectness.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:25.460
Although many viewers criticize the abrupt
ending, the unique concept of the film in

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:30.180
addition to the message behind it, makes the
film “In captivity” worthwhile.

